                <pb facs="0511" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124a/97: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Carter</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-03T15:00:00-00:44">June 3, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 3—2:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>74. Dr. Smith informed that a clear case of yellow fever has been reported next
                    to Legation premises. This is first case of the year and while under no
                    apprehensions personally am reporting the case to the diplomatic and consular
                    body in Monrovia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
